course: dictionary
lesson: 1410
title: One word, many meanings: care
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word care can be a verb or a noun, and it can mean different things. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits. «Megan could say calmly, "My mum cares for my brother."» Here cares for means looks after him.
explain: When you care about something, it matters to you. «Saying goodnight to your family shows that you care.» The clue is shows: care here means your family matters to you, not that you are looking after them.
explain: As a noun, care means serious attention, so that no mistakes or harm happen. «A pet needs food, water, care, exercise and time every day.» Try the check: swap in looking after, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Care can be a verb: to care, cares, cared, caring.
fact: Care can be a noun: care, and cares.
fact: To care about someone means they matter to you.
fact: «Handle with care» means be very careful, so that nothing gets harmed or broken.
fact: Cares are worries, the things that sit heavy on your mind.
exercise: «My mum cares for my brother.» What does cares for mean here? | Forgets | Is angry with | *Looks after
exercise: «Handle with care» is written on a box of glass. What does with care mean? | *Very carefully, so nothing gets broken | Loudly, so everyone hears | Quickly, and without stopping
exercise: «A pet needs food, water, care, exercise and time every day.» What is care in this sentence? | *Looking after, with serious attention | A kind of food | Going to bed early | A loud noise
test: «Saying goodnight to your family shows that you care.» What does you care mean? | You are angry with them | *Your family matters to you | You are going to sleep
test: «Mia shared her cares with her gran.» What are cares here? | Party plans | *Worries | Sweets
exam: «Kinship carers love the children they care for, and they can get tired.» What does care for mean in this sentence? | Ignore | Miss | Send away | *Look after, and love
